  "notes": "# Rove 0.1.18\n\n- Save large JSON response examples as workspace files from a response or when\n  creating a Case. Read the complete example in the Example tab and Documentation.\n- Create a Case from a response with a compact dialog and a choice of active or\n  fixed Environment. The full schema editor supports field rules, array limits,\n  adding or removing fields, and direct JSON edits.\n- See Base variables in the Case Variables tab. Editing a value creates a Case\n  override. Deleting the override restores the Base value in the same row.\n- Read Expected and Actual values side by side in Steps, with a failed actual\n  value highlighted.\n\nRequests that reference a JSON example file use Request format 30. Update Rove\nbefore opening a workspace that uses this format in an older client.\n\nThis beta update targets macOS Apple Silicon. The minimum supported version is 0.1.16.\n",
